@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@projectId = replace_after_create_project
@submissionId = replace_after_submit
@reviewId = replace_after_review

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Smoke test Modal endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/llm/smoke

### Create a project
# @name createProject
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "topic": "LLM-driven point cloud reasoning with verifiable geometric evidence",
  "target_standard": "paper-ready / Q1-oriented",
  "constraints": "VSCode REST Client backend test. LLM assists; PI remains final decision maker.",
  "use_llm": true,
  "fallback_on_llm_error": true,
  "students": [
    {
      "student_id": "S_JUNIOR_01",
      "name": "An",
      "level": "junior",
      "skills": ["literature review", "python basics"],
      "availability_hours_per_week": 8
    },
    {
      "student_id": "S_INTERMEDIATE_01",
      "name": "Binh",
      "level": "intermediate",
      "skills": ["python", "experiments", "data processing"],
      "availability_hours_per_week": 10
    },
    {
      "student_id": "S_STRONG_01",
      "name": "Chi",
      "level": "strong",
      "skills": ["research design", "LLM", "3D perception"],
      "availability_hours_per_week": 12
    }
  ]
}

### Copy project_id from response, then set @projectId above.

### Get package P1
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/packages/P1

### Submit package P1
# @name submitPackage
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/submissions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "package_id": "P1",
  "student_id": "S_JUNIOR_01",
  "artifact_paths": [
    "paper_cards.md",
    "dangerous_prior_art_matrix.csv",
    "gap_cards.md"
  ],
  "report_text": "# Task summary\nI created paper cards for recent work on LLM-driven point-cloud and 3D scene reasoning.\n\n# Parent research question and claim\nThis supports C1 and E1.\n\n# Method or procedure\nI searched 3D-LLM, point-cloud LLM, spatial reasoning, benchmark leakage, and tool-use terms.\n\n# Output artifacts\n- paper_cards.md\n- dangerous_prior_art_matrix.csv\n- gap_cards.md\n\n# Result interpretation\nThe stronger direction is evidence-grounded point-cloud reasoning with geometry tools, answer evidence IDs, and shortcut controls.\n\n# Limitations and confounders\nNeeds second pass on newest papers and synonym search.\n\n# Reproducibility commands\nNo code execution required. Search queries are recorded.\n\n# Next step recommendation\nPI should review dangerous prior-art and approve the contribution angle."
}

### Copy submission_id from response, then set @submissionId above.

### Review submission
# @name reviewSubmission
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/submissions/{{submissionId}}/review
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "use_llm": true,
  "fallback_on_llm_error": true
}

### Copy review_id from response, then set @reviewId above.

### Understanding gate
POST {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/reviews/{{reviewId}}/understanding
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "use_llm": true,
  "fallback_on_llm_error": true,
  "answers": [
    "Dangerous prior art is a paper that could make our contribution look incremental or already solved.",
    "The weakest gap is generic point-cloud QA because many existing 3D QA benchmarks already cover it. The stronger gap is tool-verifiable geometric reasoning with evidence IDs and shortcut controls.",
    "This package helps the PI decide whether the topic is worth pursuing by exposing closest work, novelty risks, likely reviewer objections, and required evidence."
  ]
}

### PI dashboard
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}/dashboard

### Full project state
GET {{baseUrl}}/projects/{{projectId}}
